	order_index: 6
	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["3E785FC067476803"]
			description: [
				"&6&lGregTech&r is not another tech mod. It is a different opinion about what tech mods are for."
				""
				"Everything you have built until now was a machine that does a job. GregTech gives you a &esupply chain&r: ore becomes crushed ore becomes purified ore becomes dust becomes ingot, and every one of those steps is a machine you had to build, power and feed."
				""
				"&e&lNine voltage tiers&r sit between here and the end of this chapter - Steam, LV, MV, HV, EV, IV and LuV. Each one needs the one before it. There are no shortcuts and the mod will not pretend otherwise."
				""
				"&7&lWhat you already have helps.&r Your AE2 network can drive GregTech's machines, and the PneumaticCraft assembly line taught you the shape of what is coming: recipes that a crafting grid cannot express.&r"
				""
				"&c&lThis chapter is long on purpose.&r Read the quest text - GregTech punishes guessing harder than anything else in this pack."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_machine_hull"
			id: "3EF69082A65472D5"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "003C0ABC3B762547"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 5
				}
				{
					id: "12BB76935B15094D"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 2.0d
			subtitle: "&7The long way round, deliberately"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4D74C5C009B5FA95"
				title: "Begin GregTech"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&6Nothing Here Is Free"
			x: -15.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"GregTech expects ore veins underground. You live on a floating island, so there are none."
				""
				"&e&lThe sieve is your ore vein.&r This pack adds GregTech raw ores to Ex Deorum sieve drops, tiered to match the voltage that needs them:"
				""
				"&7Crushed &fDeepslate&7 + &fdiamond mesh&7 - chalcopyrite, cassiterite, magnetite, galena, sphalerite, pyrite (steam and LV)&r"
				"&7Crushed &fBlackstone&7 + &fdiamond mesh&7 - bauxite, tetrahedrite, malachite, apatite, graphite, cinnabar&r"
				"&7Crushed &fNetherrack&7 + &fnetherite mesh&7 - garnierite, cobaltite, ilmenite, scheelite, chromite, molybdenite&r"
				"&7Crushed &fEnd Stone&7 + &fnetherite mesh&7 - cooperite, palladium, monazite, bastnasite, pitchblende, uraninite, thorium, naquadah&r"
				""
				"&e&lRaw ore, not ingots.&r That is deliberate: the whole point of GregTech is what you do to ore on the way to metal. Handing you ingots would delete the mod."
				""
				"&8Automate a sieve array before you go any further. Every tier below this one eats ore faster than the last.&r"
			]
			icon: "exdeorum:diamond_mesh"
			id: "6F928CDC354ECCAA"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "15276BF0147F517E"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 60
				}
				{
					id: "4FE9588544E9D26C"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "&7Your sieve is the ore vein"
			tasks: [{
				count: 16L
				id: "3289451AC009FE18"
				item: "gtceu:raw_chalcopyrite"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6Ore From Nothing"
			x: -15.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&c&lGregTech machines cannot be broken with a pickaxe.&r"
				""
				"&eWrench&r removes machines and rotates them. &eWire Cutter&r takes down cables. &eScrewdriver&r toggles machine settings and covers. &eHammer&r mutes machines and is a crafting ingredient everywhere. &eFile&r shapes parts."
				""
				"&7Make all five now. Trying to mine a machine without a wrench destroys it and gives you nothing back.&r"
				""
				"&8They wear out. Bronze is the starting tier; you will remake these in steel and then never think about them again.&r"
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "gtceu:bronze_wrench"
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
					GT.Tool: { }
				}
			}
