			title: "&6The Coke Oven"
			x: -12.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3885F27EA6628C90"]
			description: [
				"&6&lThe wall at the end of the steam age.&r"
				""
				"A &ePrimitive Blast Furnace&r - 3x3x4 of firebricks - takes iron and coke and gives you steel. Slowly. Very slowly."
				""
				"&7Everything in LV is made of steel. You will build several of these and they will still be the bottleneck, which is exactly why the Electric Blast Furnace later feels like such a relief.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThis pack already has six other steels&r and they are all interchangeable here - the unification script sees to that. GregTech's own recipes still want GregTech steel for machine casings, so run the furnace anyway.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:primitive_blast_furnace"
			id: "0281B22E7C755283"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "2244F588859258DC"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 80
				}
				{
					id: "07B33BE9F015CE3F"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Slow, mandatory, worth it"
			tasks: [{
				count: 16L
				id: "11E2D42E1BBA72CA"
				item: "gtceu:steel_ingot"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6&lSteel"
			x: -10.5d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0281B22E7C755283"]
			description: [
				"&6&lThe first circuit.&r Glass tube, copper wire, red alloy - crude, and the gateway to everything electric."
				""
				"&7Circuits are GregTech's real currency. There are nine tiers of them and each voltage tier needs its own. You will make thousands.&r"
				""
				"&e&lStart automating them now&r, in the steam age, before you need them by the stack. Every player who hand-crafts circuits regrets it around MV."
				""
				"&8This pack runs with harder circuit recipes enabled - the first circuit in each set yields one instead of two. Plan accordingly.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:vacuum_tube"
			id: "0E27C23D9934451A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "38589718CAA63139"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 60
			}]
			subtitle: "&7ULV - where circuits begin"
			tasks: [{
				count: 8L
				id: "506DFD7F5903199A"
				item: "gtceu:vacuum_tube"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6Vacuum Tubes"
			x: -9.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0281B22E7C755283"]
			description: [
				"Cables have to be insulated and insulation means rubber."
				""
				"&e&lRubber trees are worldgen&r, which you do not have - so this pack drops &eRubber Saplings&r from the deepslate sieve. Plant them, harvest the logs, extract the resin."
				""
				"&7Later you can make synthetic rubber from oil in a chemical reactor, which is far faster. Until then, grow trees.&r"
				""
				"&8Your PneumaticCraft refinery already produces the feedstock for the synthetic route. Worth remembering at MV.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:rubber_ingot"
			id: "71FC888AFDDA9C31"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7A9C8967CFD20826"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Saplings from the sieve"
			tasks: [{
				count: 8L
				id: "099A071C42F96BED"
				item: "gtceu:rubber_ingot"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6Rubber"
			x: -9.0d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["71FC888AFDDA9C31"]
			description: [
				"&eWire&r carries power and loses some as heat. &eCable&r is wire wrapped in rubber - less loss, and safe to touch."
				""
				"&c&lVoltage matters.&r Push LV into a machine rated for it and all is well. Push MV into an LV machine and the machine is gone."
				""
				"&7Each cable has an amperage limit too. Exceed it and the cable burns out. Thicker cable - double, quadruple, octal - carries more.&r"
				""
				"&8Tin for LV, copper for a bit more, gold and aluminium higher up. The wiremill makes them cheaply once you have one.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:copper_single_cable"
			id: "4703D75450ABD90D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7CA566D5F3EDD9B8"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Voltage kills machines"
			tasks: [
				{
					count: 4L
					id: "09AD06C72480A68D"
					item: "gtceu:tin_single_wire"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 4L
					id: "4363D8CCF691D99C"
					item: "gtceu:copper_single_cable"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6Cables and Wires"
			x: -7.5d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"A steel casing plus a cable. Every LV machine is a hull with something bolted into it."
				""
				"&7Making hulls in bulk is the single best use of your early automation. Every machine below this quest starts as one.&r"
				""
				"&8The casing tier sets the voltage tier. Steel is LV, aluminium is MV, stainless is HV, and so on up.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_machine_hull"
			id: "5667082EB6274412"
			rewards: [{
				id: "002FAD1363E5BE84"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The chassis for everything"
			tasks: [{
				count: 4L
				id: "1336B81387F00011"
				item: "gtceu:lv_machine_hull"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6LV Machine Hulls"
			x: -7.5d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&e&lLV Steam Turbine&r turns your existing boiler steam into 32 EU/t. That is the bridge from the steam age to the electric one."
				""
				"&7A &eBattery Buffer&r holds batteries and acts as your power bank - machines draw from it, generators fill it. Without one, a generator that stops means machines that stop instantly.&r"
				""
				"&c&lGregTech power is not FE.&r Nothing in Mekanism, Create or AE2 speaks EU natively. Energy Converters exist for that, and they are a later quest."
				""
				"&8One amp of LV is 32 EU/t. The battery buffer size sets how many amps you can draw at once.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_steam_turbine"
			id: "183F8AF7AFE70685"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "27C60535BF486F45"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 60
				}
				{
					id: "2600C68C617DAFFA"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "&7EU/t, amps, and why both matter"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "312302E0414E7352"
					item: "gtceu:lv_steam_turbine"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "5ADBC2EF76D8009A"
