		{
			dependencies: ["19243218E629BD4F"]
			description: [
				"Four machines that turn ingots into the shapes recipes actually ask for."
				""
				"&eBender&r makes plates and foils. &eWiremill&r makes wire. &eLathe&r makes rods, screws and bolts. &eCutter&r makes plates into smaller plates and cuts blocks."
				""
				"&7Between them these replace an enormous amount of hand-crafting. The Bender in particular ends the Forge Hammer era.&r"
				""
				"&8This pack has harder rod recipes on, so the Lathe gives one rod and dust rather than two rods. Build two lathes.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_bender"
			id: "1B1DFBFE8EBD4D7D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "58CA11B032365CDB"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Plates, wire, rods, screws"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "40AFE0707E0A3453"
					item: "gtceu:lv_bender"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "253AC9857E6546A3"
					item: "gtceu:lv_wiremill"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "201B358F882B9098"
					item: "gtceu:lv_lathe"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "2FFA7FFD8906B40C"
					item: "gtceu:lv_cutter"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6Shaping Machines"
			x: -3.0d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["19243218E629BD4F"]
			description: [
				"GregTech's chemistry is where the material tree stops being a line and becomes a web."
				""
				"&eElectrolyzer&r splits a compound into its elements - water into hydrogen and oxygen, salt into sodium and chlorine. &eCentrifuge&r separates mixtures. &eChemical Reactor&r combines things into new compounds."
				""
				"&7Almost every advanced material in the mod passes through one of these three. Synthetic rubber, plastics, and every acid you will need later start here.&r"
				""
				"&8JEI is essential from this point on. The chains get deep and nothing is guessable.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_chemical_reactor"
			id: "6ABE982B094D119A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "40892E03FE206C98"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 60
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Split, separate, combine"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "1C6DC1ACADBF7431"
					item: "gtceu:lv_chemical_reactor"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7432B63841AF998F"
					item: "gtceu:lv_electrolyzer"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "5DD13487E7EB8B8A"
					item: "gtceu:lv_centrifuge"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6First Chemistry"
			x: -3.0d
			y: 0.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["19243218E629BD4F"]
			description: [
				"&6&lThis is how one ore becomes four dust.&r"
				""
				"&e&l1.&r &7Macerator&r - raw ore into crushed ore (x2)."
				"&e&l2.&r &7Ore Washer&r - crushed ore into purified crushed ore, plus a byproduct."
				"&e&l3.&r &7Thermal Centrifuge&r - purified ore into centrifuged ore, plus another byproduct."
				"&e&l4.&r &7Macerator again&r - centrifuged ore into dust."
				""
				"&7The byproducts are the point. Chalcopyrite washed and centrifuged does not just give copper - it gives gold, and sulfur, and pyrite. Ores you sieve for one metal quietly supply three more.&r"
				""
				"&8Set this chain up once, feed everything through it, and never sieve as much again.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_ore_washer"
			id: "783ADB72710DB977"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "715318DFD185C556"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 80
				}
				{
					id: "67D3F1BB397FCE10"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7One ore, four dust, three byproducts"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7B84A18A10347BA0"
					item: "gtceu:lv_ore_washer"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "27DCB617DC55E4A9"
					item: "gtceu:lv_thermal_centrifuge"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6&lThe Full Ore Chain"
			x: -3.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1B1DFBFE8EBD4D7D"]
			description: [
				"The LV circuit. Vacuum tubes were the prototype; this is the real thing."
				""
				"&7Circuit boards, resistors, capacitors, transistors and wire, assembled together. Each of those is its own small production line.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThe Circuit Assembler exists to do all of it at once&r - it is the next quest and it is not optional if you value your time.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:basic_electronic_circuit"
			id: "27B49C89068813B9"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1BFBE146AFD7635D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 60
			}]
			subtitle: "&7LV - the first real circuit"
			tasks: [{
				count: 8L
				id: "30403ABC4E337629"
				item: "gtceu:basic_electronic_circuit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6Electronic Circuits"
			x: -1.5d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&e&lOne machine, one recipe, a finished circuit.&r"
				""
				"Feed it the components and it assembles circuits directly - no crafting grid, no intermediate juggling, and it accepts a programmed circuit to pick between recipes that share inputs."
				""
				"&7Point an AE2 Pattern Provider at it and your ME network makes circuits on demand. This is the single highest-value automation in the entire chapter.&r"
				""
				"&8Every tier from here up needs its own circuit. Automating this once pays off nine times.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_circuit_assembler"
			id: "3C16BDC13810E8A5"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "4BAAE8F2FA525F6C"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 70
				}
				{
					id: "12C5F0E9F117C120"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "&7Automate this above all else"
			tasks: [{
				id: "088BF8FF1E3B044F"
				item: "gtceu:lv_circuit_assembler"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6The Circuit Assembler"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6ABE982B094D119A"]
			description: [
				"&6&lThe machine that takes late-game crafting out of the crafting grid.&r"
				""
				"Most GregTech machine parts - motors, pistons, pumps, conveyors, robot arms, emitters, sensors, field generators - are made here, not on a bench."
				""
				"&7In this pack that is enforced: the components that define a voltage tier are assembler recipes, and they stay that way all the way to LuV. If you want a machine, you build the parts that build it.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThis is the direct descendant of your PneumaticCraft assembly line&r - same idea, nine tiers of it.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_assembler"
			id: "01B45D20008851EA"
			rewards: [
