		{
			dependencies: ["3F6135F92C4113A7"]
			description: [
				"&6&lThe machine this entire chapter was built to reach.&r"
				""
				"A long multiblock - a controller, a row of assembling units, casings, energy and fluid hatches, and a &eData Access Hatch&r holding the research."
				""
				"&e&lIt does not accept recipes. It accepts research.&r You scan an item into a Data Stick with a Scanner, feed the stick to the line, and only then can it build that item. Nothing about it fits in a crafting grid, a machine GUI, or an AE2 pattern without deliberate work."
				""
				"&7&lThis is the payoff.&r Every high-tier component from here to the end of GregTech is an assembly line recipe. Automating it - feeding materials, managing data sticks, driving it from your ME network - is the real endgame of the mod, and it is exactly the skill PneumaticCraft's little assembly line was teaching you eight tiers ago.&r"
				""
				"&8Build it long. The number of assembling units sets how complex a recipe it can run.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:assembly_line"
			id: "33492215FCC0998C"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "0C5F4D9A2DE8789D"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 10
				}
				{
					id: "7D2CA84D94432E7A"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 2.0d
			subtitle: "&7Research, then manufacture"
			tasks: [{
				id: "182B26A1FFB3C3F1"
				item: "gtceu:assembly_line"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6&lThe Assembly Line"
			x: 15.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&c&lThe rarest thing in the sieve.&r One percent from crushed end stone with a netherite mesh."
				""
				"&7Naquadah is the LuV material and the reason the End Stone tier of the sieve bridge exists at all. Expect to run a very large sieve array for a very long time.&r"
				""
				"&e&lEnriching it&r in a centrifuge gives Naquadah Enriched, which is what the high-tier alloys actually want.&r"
				""
				"&8If this feels punishing, that is intentional - it is the last material gate in the chapter.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:naquadah_ingot"
			id: "33F1BBD37C4B8F86"
