			x: 16.5d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&6&lYou started with a sieve and a crook. You finished with an assembly line running on naquadah.&r"
				""
				"Nine voltage tiers. Four coil temperatures. An ore chain that turns one raw ore into four dust and three byproducts. Circuits grown from crystal. A manufacturing line that has to be taught what to build before it will build it."
				""
				"&7&lNothing in this chapter could be crafted on a bench&r, and that was the whole point. GregTech is the late game of this pack because it is the only mod here where the answer to 'how do I make this' is always another factory.&r"
				""
				"&e&lWhat is left:&r ZPM, UV and the Fusion Reactor, none of which this chapter holds your hand through. And the Heart of the Sky, which is still waiting in Act IV.&r"
				""
				"&8Go and automate something.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:luv_machine_hull"
			id: "6078D2EFDD1403C3"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "535B21E7B1493383"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 20
				}
				{
					id: "1D23477B8BECAE87"
					type: "random"
				}
				{
					id: "227634917B725190"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 2.0d
			subtitle: "&7GregTech mastered"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3EA02109F7C5F871"
					item: "gtceu:luv_machine_hull"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "42B7959402F46321"
					item: "gtceu:assembly_line"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6&lIndustry"
			x: 18.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["19243218E629BD4F"]
			description: [
				"&c&lThe single most confusing item in GregTech, and you need it constantly.&r"
				""
				"Many recipes share the same inputs and differ only in output. One ingot in an Extruder could become a rod, a plate, a wire or a gear - the machine has no way to know which you meant."
				""
				"&e&lThe Programmed Circuit is how you tell it.&r Set it to a number, put it in the machine's circuit slot, and that number selects the recipe. JEI shows which number each recipe wants."
				""
				"&7It is never consumed. One per machine, set once, forgotten forever.&r"
				""
				"&8If a machine refuses a recipe you are certain is correct, this is almost always why.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:programmed_circuit"
			id: "17A2DE7D7DA93E23"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4688B0A65FFC772A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7How machines know what you meant"
			tasks: [{
				id: "41B5F7530CF64D0A"
				item: "gtceu:programmed_circuit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&e&lThe Programmed Circuit"
			x: -4.5d
			y: 5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3CF8A5492C9EB3DB"]
			description: [
				"&e&lGregTech machines have no input or output sides until you give them one.&r"
				""
				"Right-click a machine face with a &eConveyor Module&r and it becomes an item port. A &ePump&r makes it a fluid port. A &eRobot Arm&r does the same with filtering and exact-count control."
				""
				"&7Screwdriver-click the cover to set direction, mode and filters. This is how GregTech automates - not with pipes into the block, but with covers on the block.&r"
				""
				"&8Covers also do redstone logic, machine control and readouts. There are a lot of them and they are worth browsing.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_conveyor_module"
			id: "3EC427A37E19E448"
			rewards: [{
				id: "459F2C1511A1BED6"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 60
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Automation lives on the faces"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "1A31BA45FC4F78ED"
					item: "gtceu:lv_conveyor_module"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "2445D2374C3708D7"
					item: "gtceu:lv_electric_pump"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "108C3CFB65CFDAE1"
					item: "gtceu:lv_robot_arm"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&e&lMachine Covers"
			x: -3.0d
			y: 5.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Item and fluid pipes, in sizes from tiny to huge."
				""
				"&7Bigger pipe moves more per tick. Item pipes have a throughput limit and fluid pipes have both a rate and a temperature limit - move something hot through a low-grade pipe and it melts.&r"
				""
				"&e&lRestrictive item pipes&r are ignored by routing unless there is no alternative - the standard trick for controlling where items actually go.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:copper_normal_fluid_pipe"
			id: "56B58ADAC7845CFF"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2AC84031BAAC2467"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Rate, temperature, and melting"
			tasks: [
				{
					count: 4L
					id: "397B0215DC6C1AC7"
					item: "gtceu:tin_normal_item_pipe"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 4L
					id: "250A56F492C14301"
					item: "gtceu:copper_normal_fluid_pipe"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&ePipes"
			x: -1.5d
			y: 5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["35C0E27B8CC84BB1"]
			description: [
				"&e&lThe most important number in GregTech is the one on the recipe, not the machine.&r"
				""
				"Every recipe has a voltage and a duration. Run it in a machine of exactly that tier and you get exactly that duration."
				""
				"&7Run it in a machine one tier higher and it takes &ehalf&r the time for &efour times&r the power per tick. Two tiers up: a quarter of the time, sixteen times the power. This is called an overclock and it applies everywhere.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThe consequence:&r a high-tier machine is not just faster, it is dramatically less power-efficient per operation. Sometimes the right answer is more LV machines, not one EV machine."
				""
				"&8Multiblocks with parallel processing sidestep this entirely, which is why they dominate the late game.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:mv_electric_motor"
			id: "0EE8448366B93CF1"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1EC5648B663F9E58"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 60
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Half the time, four times the power"
			tasks: [{
				count: 2L
				id: "12E8DF48FFBA2199"
				item: "gtceu:mv_electric_motor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&e&lOverclocking"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 5.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Multiblocks do not have item slots. They have &ehatches&r and &ebuses&r that you build into the wall."
				""
				"&7&eBus&r moves items, &ehatch&r moves fluid, &eenergy hatch&r brings power in. Each one replaces one casing block in the structure.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThe hatch tier caps the multiblock's voltage.&r An LV energy hatch on an EV multiblock means it runs at LV."
				""
				"&8Most multiblocks accept several buses. More buses means more parallel input, which matters enormously later.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_input_bus"
			id: "423AC14C76774FF1"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F46C45777895A0F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7How multiblocks eat"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "2616F0FE1A8753E4"
					item: "gtceu:lv_input_bus"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "71A3CA42D583749D"
					item: "gtceu:lv_output_bus"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "291B93459D5851E5"
